Z||000003||Rob Durham||07-22-2001||10:02 AM||||The distributor could be 180 deg out, that would cause the same symptoms your talking about||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||07-22-2001||10:18 AM||||What carb are you using? I'm wondering if lowering the float level was a good course of action.<BR>The fuel pressure can always be turned back up if necessary if indications of fuel starvation are present.<BR>Have you checked both the primary and secondary ignition circuits to insure both are working? Also is the ignition solid state or are you using points?||||reg||1
